course: dictionary
lesson: 7844
title: Radar: finding things with waves
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Radar is a system that finds things you cannot see easily. It sends out radio waves, then catches them when they bounce back. The time they take to return tells the radar how far away something is, and changes in the waves tell it how fast the thing is moving.
explain: «Venus is wrapped in thick clouds that hide its surface completely from ordinary telescopes; its surface was mapped by radar.» Light cannot pass through those clouds, but radio waves can. Radar let scientists draw a map of the ground hidden underneath.
explain: Radar is also a word for a kind of machine, as in «weather radar», and a phrase: «on someone's radar» means they know about it or are paying attention to it. Try swapping that phrase into a sentence: «The coach has your name on her radar» means she is watching you.
fact: Radar stands for radio detection and ranging.
fact: Radar sends out radio waves and catches them when they bounce back.
fact: Radar is used to find planes, ships, storms and cars, and to work out how fast they move.
fact: «Radar» can also mean machines that find enemy planes in the dark, as in the Second World War.
fact: «On someone's radar» means they are being noticed or paid attention to.
exercise: «Radar sends out radio waves and catches them when they bounce back.» What does radar catch? | *Radio waves that bounce back | Rain drops falling from the sky | Sound from a whistle | Light from the stars
exercise: What is radar used for? | To grow carrots in the dark | *To find where planes, ships and storms are | To bake bread and cakes | To make music louder
exercise: «Police use radar to catch speeding cars.» What does the radar help the police find out? | What colour the car is | Who is driving the car on Sunday | *How fast a car is moving | Whether the car is new
test: «Bracken Cave in Texas has millions of bats, a cloud so big it shows on weather radar.» Why does the bat cloud show on weather radar? | The bats sing loudly to the radar | *The cloud is so big that its waves bounce back to the radar | Bats glow in the dark | The radar is a bat-shaped machine
test: The teacher says, «Jake is on my radar now.» What does this mean? | Jake is lost in the school | Jake has gone home early | *She is paying attention to Jake
exam: Which best describes radar? | A machine that only makes sound | A type of carrot that helps you see in the dark | *A system that uses radio waves to find where things are and how fast they move | A kind of bird that flies at night
